{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5e3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae3f-54f0-7453-97f2-3b7774743ad2"},"sequence":332,"recorded_at":1780531400000659,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"932cad06-180f-40c2-8da9-e768b00b3c3d","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"932cad06-180f-40c2-8da9-e768b00b3c3d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"932cad06-180f-40c2-8da9-e768b00b3c3d"},"call_id":"call_01a0ae3fde1175e4a7149fd7c737d06f","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-z1yxg9/TASK-260830-z1yxg9_results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-z1yxg9 results — RPC envelope/hello + Host Channel 1.0.0\n2|\n3|Role: developer. Branch work left UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for handoff snapshot.\n4|\n5|## Deliverable\n6|\n7|- `internal/rpcwire` completed for RPC 5.0.0: exact RPC-4 envelope/body shapes,\n8|  25-key hello maps with `contracts.rpc` `[\"5.0.0\"]`, 8 namespaces,\n9|  namespace/cardinality validation, offered-limit floors, historical\n10|  Structured Error framing (statically 1.3.0 for RPC majors 4 and 5 via a\n11|  new `axerror` binding row), 8 MiB line bound, exact fixtures, refusal\n12|  table, fuzz target.\n13|- `internal/hostchannel` (new): Host Channel 1.0.0 over RPC 5.0.0 —\n14|  mutual TLS 1.3 (`ax-host/1`, enrolled roots only, no tickets/cache/\n15|  resumption), enrolled-identity supplement, authorized hello both roles,\n16|  current-generation dispatch and mutation boundaries, specified Error\n17|  1.3.0 refusal framing, Configuration-4 launch selection.\n18|- Traceability gaps (11.2/11.3/11.8/11.9/11.10/15.1/15.3), README,\n19|  LOGBOOK, and the `task-board.config.json` fuzz gate updated.\n20|\n21|## AC accounting: 7 of 7 rows driven through production entries\n22|\n23|| # | Row | Production call sites | Named tests |\n24|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n25|| 1 | Request/response correlation | `hostchannel.Dial` + `Call` + `Serve` | TestFullHandshakeHelloAndOperation, TestHelloResponseCorrelation |\n26|| 2 | Hello maps and nonce echo | `Serve`/`Dial` hello exchange | TestFullHandshakeHelloAndOperation, TestRefusesInvalidHello/* |\n27|| 3 | Inventory namespace/cardinality | `Call(\"inventory.roots\")` dispatch | TestInventoryRootsThroughChannel |\n28|| 4 | Offered limits | hello validation both roles | TestFullHandshakeHelloAndOperation, TestOversizeHelloLine |\n29|| 5 | Historical Structured Error framing | `Serve` refusal frames, `Dial` mapping | TestRefusesNonHelloBeforeHello, TestHelloFailureMapping/* |\n30|| 6 | Bilateral admission before dispatch | `AuthorizeDispatch` at hello both roles | TestRefusesHelloUUIDMismatch, TestRefusesServerHelloUUIDMismatch, TestRefusesNotAllowlisted, TestRefusesDestinationMismatch |\n31|| 7 | Deadlines and generation recovery | bounded reads/writes, stale gates, `WatchGeneration` | TestHelloDeadline/*, TestHelloWriteDeadline, TestDispatchTimeout, TestStaleGenerationAtDispatch/*, TestStaleGenerationAtMutation, TestDispatchExpiryClosesWithoutFrame, TestWatchGeneration |\n32|\n33|Crash/idempotency: the channel writes no durable state (static + runtime\n34|censuses), so no crash-recovery behavior is attested; trust commits stay\n35|atomic in hosttrust. No unsupported capability is advertised: no `ax`\n36|command, SSH launch, provider plugin, or object exchange exists.\n37|\n38|## Validation (this run, worktree HEAD ae5a4cc)\n39|\n40|- `go test ./... -count=1`: all packages ok, exit 0.\n41|- `go test ./internal/rpcwire ./internal/hostchannel -race -count=1`: ok.\n42|- Coverage: hostchannel 81.6%, rpcwire 97.8%.\n43|- `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, gofmt check: clean.\n44|- Fuzz gate `FuzzUntrustedEnvelopes` 100x: PASS.\n45|- Traceability suite + README figures pin: green with reviewed digest\n46|  `5102d3bce23e6f27264232332a300dbb89237dc7792673efe9ec039b1219ce08`.\n47|- Mutants: hostchannel 1 neutral passed + 22 narrowing killed + 1\n48|  documented harmless SURVIVED (client-cache); rpcwire 1 neutral passed\n49|  + 34 narrowing killed (incl. v5-exact). Token-preserving\n50|  census-evasion mutant passes the static census and is killed by the\n51|  runtime census with the full suite running. Tables: see outcome tar.\n52|\n53|## Conformance matrix\n54|\n55|See `TASK-260830-z1yxg9_conformance-matrix.md`: every HC-* gate with its\n56|positive/negative vectors, production entries, and killing mutants.\n57|\n58|## Restoration\n59|\n60|See `TASK-260830-z1yxg9_restoration.md`: 10 of 11 untracked packet files\n61|restored verbatim with matching sha256; UNRESOLVED_QUESTIONS dropped as\n62|superseded; 4 tracked deltas re-applied by hand onto the v0.6.0 tree.\n63|\n64|## Stated bounds\n65|\n66|- SSH-carrier parity by construction (abstract Stream, no SSH-impl\n67|  branch); no live SSH carrier test.\n68|- Async one-second invalidation close is the caller's `WatchGeneration`\n69|  poll; boundaries (dispatch/send/mutation) are enforced in-package.\n70|- TLS alert bytes owned by crypto/tls (asserted shape: alert-or-close,\n71|  never JSON).\n72|- 1 MiB handshake cap proven at the exact unit boundary; Go's 256 KiB\n73|  message cap fires first end to end (documented, integration-bounded).\n74|- Traceability: gap texts updated; coverage levels and clause\n75|  enumerations unchanged, no new clause discharge claimed.\n76|- Pre-existing worktree `.task-board/` checkout noise (34 files) predates\n77|  this run and was not touched.\n78|\n79|## Handoff\n80|\n81|Ready for review. Candidate paths: `internal/rpcwire/`,\n82|`internal/hostchannel/`, `internal/axerror/binding.go` (+test),\n83|`internal/traceability/`, `README.md`, `LOGBOOK.md`,\n84|`task-board.config.json`. No commit was made on the Story branch.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
